LZW data compression
====================

Part of CACHE_FRAMEWORK: the same kernels as A653_Benchmarks, kept as a
separate set for cache studies (cache locking and cache-miss analysis). The
algorithm is identical to A653_Benchmarks/Compress unless noted below.

What it tests
-------------

Execution time of a memory- and branch-intensive compression loop (a hash table
lookup per input byte).

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with one periodic process.

Compresses a 20 KB buffer of random data with the LZW algorithm of the UNIX
compress utility (from SPEC95), using a 257-entry hash table. Period and time
capacity: 10 s.

Expected output
---------------

"Compressing text of 20480 elements" every period.

Notes
-----

The input buffer is filled once in main(), not every period.
The hash index is reduced modulo the table size: the original code indexed far
outside htab (undefined behaviour), which faulted on 64-bit targets.

Origin
------

Ported from Malardalen WCET benchmarks
(http://www.mrtc.mdh.se/projects/wcet/benchmarks.html).

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/Compress/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/Compress/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
